Given a list of strings, write a function to group anagrams together. Anagrams are words that contain the same characters in any order. Your function should handle Unicode characters and treat uppercase and lowercase letters as the same when determining anagrams.

Reference Solution (Wrong)
```python
def group_anagrams(words):
    anagrams = {}
    for word in words:
        sorted_word = ''.join(sorted(word))
        if sorted_word in anagrams:
            anagrams[sorted_word].append(word)
        else:
            anagrams[sorted_word] = [word]
    return

