Develop a recursive function to flatten a nested list of integers into a single list. The input list can have any level of nesting. `[1, [2, [3, 4], 5], 6, [7, 8]]`<|im_end|>
<|im_start|>assistant
```python
def flatten(nested_list):
    result = []
    for element<mask> nested<mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask> result.extend(flatten(element))
        else:
            result.append(element)
    return result

#<mask> usage<mask><mask>_list<mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask><mask>

