A list of integers is provided. Write a function to find the contiguous subarray (containing at least one number) which has the largest sum and return its sum, considering that the list can be circular. Implement a solution that efficiently handles this case.

Reference Solution (Wrong)
```python
def max_subarray_sum(nums):
    max_current = max_global = nums[0]
    for i in range(1, len(nums)):
        max_current = max(nums[i], max_current + nums[i])
        if max_current > max_global:
            max_global = max_current

