Given a linked list, write a function to detect if there is a cycle in the list and return the starting node of the cycle. If there is no cycle, return `None`. You may not modify the linked list.

Reference Solution (Wrong)
```python
def detectCycle(head):
    slow = head
    fast = head
    while fast and fast.next:
        slow = slow.next
        fast = fast.next.next
        if slow == fast:
            return slow
    return None
```
