Given a linked list, determine if it has a cycle that starts at a node which is at an even index when counting from the head node, and the cycle length must be an odd number. Implement the function `hasCycleStartingAtEvenIndexWithOddLength(ListNode head)` which returns `true` if there is such a cycle and `false` otherwise.

Reference Solution (Wrong)
```python
def hasCycleStartingAtEvenIndexWithOddLength(head):
    slow = fast = head
    while fast and fast.next:
        slow = slow.next
        fast = fast

